Subject: [mbb-compat] Restore format_args_nl and Utf8Chunks::new for rustc >= 1.79+

rustc removed the internal builtin macro `format_args_nl` and never exposed a
public `Utf8Chunks::new` constructor. Reintroduce the former as a macro_rules
wrapper with identical semantics (format_args! + trailing newline) at the base
crate root so every module and downstream macro sees it, and construct chunks
via the stable `<[u8]>::utf8_chunks()` accessor instead.

Applies on top of 0001-0010 (import-block context matches post-0009 state).

--- a/native/src/base/lib.rs
+++ b/native/src/base/lib.rs
@@ -3,6 +3,18 @@
 #![feature(io_error_more)]
 #![feature(utf8_chunks)]
 
+// Compat: rustc no longer exports the internal builtin macro
+// `format_args_nl`. Provide an equivalent macro_rules wrapper: the same
+// expansion as format_args! with a trailing newline. Defined at the crate
+// root before all module declarations so every mod sees it textually.
+macro_rules! format_args_nl {
+    ($($arg:tt)*) => {
+        format_args!("{}\n", format_args!($($arg)*))
+    };
+}
+
+// Compat: base/cstr.rs now constructs Utf8Chunks via the stable
+// `<[u8]>::utf8_chunks()` accessor (see cstr.rs hunk in this patch).
 pub use const_format;
 pub use libc;
 use num_traits::FromPrimitive;
